  "summary": "DIY anti-fashion: safety pins, tartan bondage trousers, leather, torn tees and slogan graphics weaponized as style.",
  "description": "Vivienne Westwood and Malcolm McLaren's shop SEX outfitted London punk in ripped tees (\"Destroy\"), mohawks, chains and bondage straps while NYC protopunks wore leather and attitude. Punk fashion is deliberate garbage-chic: shredded, pinned, studded, marker-scribbled, ripped from class anger and art-school provocation. Its graphics — Jamie Reid's ransom-note cutouts — rewired graphic design. Every later alt scene quotes its grammar.",
